Elysia plugin factory (BR-014-01/07 — server-side enforcement, not just
UI gating). `.use(requirePermissionPlugin())` derives `authUser` on the
context for every route registered after it; combine with
`.guard({}, (app) => app.get(..., handler))` per-route, or call
`requirePermission(permission)` inside a handler body — see usage below.

Usage pattern (per-route explicit check — preferred, keeps 404-vs-403
anti-enumeration decisions in the route's own hands per BR-014-08):

```ts
const app = new Elysia()
  .use(requirePermissionPlugin())
  .get("/api/v1/admin/foo", ({ authUser }) => {
    requirePermission(authUser, "admin.access");
    return { ok: true };
  });
```

